# Cloudflare Pages rewrite rules. Read docs/2026-08-16-platform-config-playbook.md §2.1
# before you change this file.
# - "/" is now a real pre-rendered landing page, not an empty shell.
# - A client route never rewrites to "/". That would serve the landing
#   page and its content, then swap to the real page after the bundle
#   boots. Users open /verify-email and /auth/complete from an email
#   link, so this failure is visible on first paint.
# - A client route rewrites to "/app/" instead. That directory holds a
#   copy of the client-render shell Angular emits as index.csr.html. The
#   "ngcm" body attribute in the shell tells Angular to switch hydration
#   off, so it never fights a DOM that does not match the booted route.
# - The destination is "/app/", never "/index.csr.html". Pages turns a
#   destination that contains "index" into a clean-URL 308, the same way
#   it does for "/index.html". "/app/" is already a directory index, so
#   Pages has nothing to normalise.
# - Every client route needs a row, plus its trailing-slash twin.
# - A path with no row falls through to 404.html.
# - Test only on a real preview deployment (--branch=preview). "wrangler pages dev"
#   cannot parse these rules correctly.
# - A pre-rendered route (/, /pricing, /terms, /privacy) must not have a row here.
#   A row would rewrite its real HTML file back to the shell and undo pre-rendering.
# - scripts/check-redirects.mjs enforces both rules above at build time.
/login /app/ 200
/login/ /app/ 200
/signup /app/ 200
/signup/ /app/ 200
/verify-email /app/ 200
/verify-email/ /app/ 200
/auth/complete /app/ 200
/auth/complete/ /app/ 200
/reset-password /app/ 200
/reset-password/ /app/ 200
/reset-password/confirm /app/ 200
/reset-password/confirm/ /app/ 200
/dashboard /app/ 200
/dashboard/ /app/ 200
/assessments/* /app/ 200
/sites/* /app/ 200
/account /app/ 200
/account/ /app/ 200
